{"title":"2025 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the coordinates of the point of intersection of the lines with equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d653c62693362a0aa869a02ae7619c0e5354a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3x + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/3598674da80fb95e53d410448c693feb3b3f5710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 7x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When two lines intersect, their <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinates are equal. Thus, we can equate the equations of the two lines to find the intersection:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77be7c7779211b47a2fd8feb532220333f13b396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3x + 7 = 7x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf419b419efe1709dcbc59c2f4a23d65337e73e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 3 = 7x - 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5af4e983aea8c64675136edea3d073555786137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cae66478bdade2e3c6903d3c479e322d0745f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{4}{4} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>To find out the y-coordinate, we can now plug-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> into one of the equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc2471c4dcad95eb183bd5348cd90871e6a147b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3 \\times 1 + 7 = 3 + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e39017825b13dffed7dd44a9aa8760f7d9382f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Because the x-coordinate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the y-coordinate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the intersection point has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d99a4ce0a22337a3d603a4fe397ab5832b7aa5f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(1, 10)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 56/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2517/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.789      1 2025_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.789      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34991:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018031843 and revision id 279567. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}